  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Institutionalizing Non-Communicable Disease implementation research</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) Support the generation of locally relevant evidence and institutionalization of strengthened national capacities in Low- and Middle-Income countries (LMICs). 2) Enhance the impact of these efforts by embedding them within ongoing Non-Communicable Disease (NCD) programmes and strengthen institutional capacity. 3) Contribute to strengthening a global community committed to employing NCD implementation research to improve health outcomes and achieve Sustainable Development Goal target 3.4.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A collaboration between the World Health Organization (WHO) Alliance for Health Policy and Systems Research (AHPSR) and the National Institute for Health and Care Research (NIHR) to support a call for proposals for low- and middle-income country (LMIC) research teams to conduct Non-Communicable Disease (NCD) implementation research to combine a range of essential health services into a coordinated and comprehensive system, with a primary care setting as the central point of access for individuals and communities. This collaboration will support four new LMIC country research teams and the scale up of existing programmes of work in India, Nepal, Ghana and Ethiopia.</narrative>
  </description>
